00:57:23,478 --> 00:57:29,478
Mank is a 2020 American biographical drama film about screenwriter Herman J.

11
01:03:07,826 --> 01:03:13,826
Mankiewicz and his development of the screenplay for
Orson Welles's 1941 film Citizen Kane.

12
01:08:52,173 --> 01:08:58,173
It was directed by David Fincher based on a screenplay written by his late father Jack
Fincher and was produced by Ceán Chaffin, Douglas Urbanski, and Eric Roth.

13
01:14:36,521 --> 01:14:42,521
It stars Gary Oldman in the title role, alongside Amanda Seyfried, Lily Collins, Arliss Howard, Tom Pelphrey, Sam Troughton, Ferdinand
Kingsley, Tuppence Middleton, Tom Burke, Joseph Cross, Jamie McShane, Toby Leonard Moore, Monika Gossman, and Charles Dance.

14
01:20:20,869 --> 01:20:26,869
Fincher originally intended to make Mank after he completed The Game (1997), with Kevin
Spacey and Jodie Foster as the leads, but the project did not come to fruition.

15
01:26:05,217 --> 01:26:11,217
Eventually, the project was officially announced in July 2019, and filming took
place around Los Angeles from November 2019 to February 2020.

16
01:31:49,565 --> 01:31:55,565
To pay homage to the films of the 1930s, Mank was shot
in black-and-white, using RED cameras.

17
01:37:33,913 --> 01:37:39,913
Mank had a limited theatrical release on November 13, 2020,
and began streaming on Netflix on December 4.

18
01:43:18,260 --> 01:43:24,260
The film received positive reviews from critics, who praised Fincher's direction, as well as the acting
(particularly Oldman and Seyfried), cinematography, production values, and musical score.

19
01:49:02,608 --> 01:49:08,608
The film earned the leading ten nominations at the 93rd Academy Awards, including Best Picture, Best Director, Best Actor
(Oldman), and Best Supporting Actress (Seyfried), and won for Best Production Design and Best Cinematography.

20
01:54:46,956 --> 01:54:52,956
It received the leading six nominations at the 78th Golden Globe Awards, including Best Motion
Picture – Drama as well as the six nominations at the 74th British Academy Film Awards.

21
02:00:31,304 --> 02:00:37,304
The film explores themes of movie business, screenwriter,
biography, hollywood, black and white.

22
02:06:15,652 --> 02:06:21,652
The tone is emotional.
